From 9900a81b25f63c57412ec56018ae36a2180ebbe5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhl <nhl@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:58:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/42] NHL: nhl_upload_prepass - record uploads of pages not
 yet accessed in the submission into a pre-pass (default off)

Uploads from RequestRanges end the render pass (SubmitBarriers before the copy) - the largest
source of render pass breaks per frame. When none of an upload's pages was requested (read,
written or uploaded) earlier in the current submission, the copy is recorded into a separate
deferred command buffer that runs before the main stream, between two whole-buffer barriers.
Pages requested in the submission are tracked in a bitmap via the new SharedMemory::RangesRequested
hook. [nhl-prepass] logs prepass/inline uploads per second.
